## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates expertise in per-tenant event-time semantics, SLA-bound late data handling, and scalable state management in KCNA under multi-tenant workloads.

## Key Concepts

- Event-time processing with tenant-specific watermarks
- Per-tenant state stores and partitioning strategies
- Late data handling within SLA constraints
- Fault tolerance through checkpointing and recovery
- At-least-once delivery guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: per-tenant watermark advancement and late event routing
class TenantWindowManager {
  constructor() {
    this.watermark = -Infinity;
    this.windows = new Map();
  }

  onEvent(tenantId, event) {
    const isLate = event.timestamp < this.watermark;
    if (isLate) {
      this.routeToDeadLetterQueue(tenantId, event);
    } else {
      this.mergeIntoActiveWindow(tenantId, event);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle backpressure when tenants have varying event volumes?
- What strategies would you implement to optimize state store compaction?
- How do you ensure watermark fairness across tenants with different latency budgets?

